flowchart TB
    accTitle: BlaBla architecture
    accDescr: The CLI and project layer compose two independent verification pipelines: behavior parsing and typed IR feed a finite campaign through the trusted application adapter; structure parsing feeds static source providers and one fact evaluator. finish combines fresh canonical behavior and live structure into OVERALL. Alongside them, memory feeds queries, task records feed deterministic challenge, and explicit host checkpoints feed bounded expert policy and optional advice. These non-gating surfaces never decide completion.
    entry["CLI + project composition"]
    entry --> behavior["Behavior<br/>parser → typed IR"]
    entry --> structure["Structure<br/>parser → fact evaluator"]
    behavior --> campaign["Finite campaign<br/>coverage + shrinking"]
    campaign <--> app["Trusted adapter<br/>JSON Lines application"]
    structure <--> providers["Static source providers<br/>Python · Rust · TS/JS<br/>Go · Java · C/C++"]
    campaign --> result["finish → OVERALL<br/>fresh behavior + live structure"]
    structure --> result
    entry -. "non-gating" .-> memory["Registered memory<br/>status / explain"]
    memory --> tasks["Task records<br/>deterministic challenge"]
    tasks -. "selected context" .-> expert["Observed host checkpoint<br/>packet → provider → policy<br/>optional bounded advice"]
    classDef gate fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#15803d,color:#14532d;
    class result gate;
